WEBVTT

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:40.320
Shuurei continues to urge the joukan to get jobs wherever they can, to avoid getting fired.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:45.660
Only half a month remains until the deadline.

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:56.260
I only have half a month left.

00:01:56.260 --> 00:01:59.050
Oh, are you feeling down?

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.050
Tan-tan...

00:02:01.910 --> 00:02:06.370
I heard some places are starting to employ a few of the joukan.

00:02:06.370 --> 00:02:07.310
Aren't you glad?

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:10.890
Sure I am, but they're so harsh.

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:13.320
They've started boasting about it.

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:16.320
So, what about you?

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:19.690
Tan-tan, you're mean.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:21.780
You're gonna say I'm too soft-hearted, aren't you?

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:22.960
Yes.

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:26.200
You've put off dealing with your own issues. What are you gonna do now?

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:30.460
But I'm impressed too.

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:31.830
Eh?

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:38.800
I thought for sure you'd abandon them halfway, but you've put up with the joukan this far.

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:41.470
Tan-tan, are you being cynical?

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:43.950
No, I'm honestly impressed.

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:47.660
You haven't given up on yourself either, have you?

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:53.730
Well, you're different from the others. You must have some offers by now?

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:56.440
Well, yes, but...

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:58.030
But what?

00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:01.110
Nothing.

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:04.400
Fine. If you say so.

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:07.490
What's that for?

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:11.130
Ah! I thought I'd play it for a change.

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:18.260
Hey, if I ask, will you play a piece for me?

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:19.040
What?

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:21.380
Sure, of course.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:24.510
Do you have a request?

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:25.760
Anything.

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:29.020
Okay.

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:30.240
Then...

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:47.710
You're here again?

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:54.750
Riou, can I talk to you about me today?

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:57.000
You mean "today again," right?

00:03:57.610 --> 00:04:01.630
I'm... in love with this woman-

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:04.640
Ah, it's impossible. Give it up, forget about her.

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:04.640
Ah... uh...

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:07.820
Why are you so harsh?!

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:09.310
I haven't told you anything about it!

00:04:10.910 --> 00:04:15.150
Come on. If you fancy a woman, all you need to do is bring her to the Imperial Residence.

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:18.980
But you haven't, which means she's a woman you can't approach easily, right?

00:04:20.890 --> 00:04:24.170
I'm doing my best.

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:29.750
That sound...

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:31.110
Shuurei...

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:40.950
The woman you're in love with... is Kou Shuurei?

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:43.040
Yeah.

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:46.260
She's a difficult girl.

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:48.750
Wh-What? Why is that?!

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:53.270
It's not manly to ask about a woman's secrets behind her back!

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:59.470
Hmm, as I'd expect from a ghost...

00:04:59.470 --> 00:05:00.980
Your words are very respectable.

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:02.720
A ghost?

00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:04.800
Aren't you?

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:08.660
You thought I was a ghost?

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:10.690
You're not?

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:13.830
This library is famous for having ghosts.

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:17.020
Besides, you know everything and have a quick mind.

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:19.350
You can't possibly be an ordinary child.

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:22.960
On top of it, you have the same name as Hyou Riou, whom I met the other day.

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:24.580
You even have a similar air about you.

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:29.680
You must be his ancestor, definitely.

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:34.180
Seriously, you think a ghost would read books and eat snacks?

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:36.630
You're eating my offerings.

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:40.040
Idiot!

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:43.170
I'm alive, and Hyou Riou is my father.

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:44.820
Of course we look alike!

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:45.980
Father?!

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:50.570
No way! He didn't look that much older than me!

00:05:50.570 --> 00:05:52.080
How old was he when you were born?!

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:54.740
He might look young, but if I'm right, he's over eighty!

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:59.090
You must've heard that some Hyou family members seem to have perpetual youth and longevity.

00:05:59.510 --> 00:06:01.040
My father's like that.

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:04.430
Eighty? With that appearance?!

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:09.050
But he looked so young and... handsome.

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:12.150
Next time you see him, give him a shoulder massage.

00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:13.560
He'll like it.

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:17.430
If you're not a ghost, then what are you doing in Kiyou?

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:20.040
Oh, you haven't heard?

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:20.950
What?

00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:23.070
Nothing. You'll find out later.

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:37.770
You're good.

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:39.460
Even I can tell.

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:41.960
You have a lot of talents, don't you?

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:45.960
Tan-tan, did something happen?

00:06:46.430 --> 00:06:49.000
Nothing, really.

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:51.840
Tomorrow's a day off, isn't it?

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:54.640
See ya. Take care on your way home.

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:57.970
Tan-tan's acting strange.

00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:02.360
The Civil Service, the Department of Finance, the Department of Education...

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:09.080
Like Tan-tan said, I should probably choose from one of those.

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:10.910
But...

00:07:12.270 --> 00:07:15.740
when the other joukan are working so hard to get a job,

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:21.080
can I really take the easy path and then face them proudly in the future?

00:07:23.690 --> 00:07:26.750
No, I can't be particular at this moment.

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:29.520
What's important right now is to remain an official.

00:07:29.980 --> 00:07:33.060
I have no time left. I should just go and bow my head...

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:38.970
You tell others to take the hard way,
yet you'll let yourself take the easy path?

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:48.560
Well, that's fine by me.

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:52.700
It means that you've reached your limit.

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:53.950
What?

00:07:56.270 --> 00:07:57.950
Umm, who are you?

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:10.190
I can't sleep...

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:16.430
Yet you'll let yourself take the easy path?

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:21.230
That's it! Stop it!

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:24.940
I keep on thinking because I'm laying awake here in bed!

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:48.760
The salt... feels grainy.

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:55.110
Is Seiran still asleep?

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:57.010
Good morning, Shuurei.

00:08:57.010 --> 00:08:58.510
Good morning, Father.

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:02.140
Seiran hasn't come home since yesterday.

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:03.220
What?

00:09:03.220 --> 00:09:07.080
But today's a day off. Is he that busy?

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:13.360
The price has gone up again.

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:15.450
Yes, Shuurei-chan.

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:22.250
But rather than saying, "It's gone up,"
it'd be more appropriate to say, "It had to go up."

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:24.090
What do you mean by that?

00:09:25.720 --> 00:09:30.000
I thought you would've noticed, but there's quite a lot of white sand mixed in, right?

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:30.790
Yes.

00:09:30.790 --> 00:09:32.550
That's when this came in handy.

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:33.300
What?

00:09:33.570 --> 00:09:35.420
You pour the salt in here.

00:09:48.840 --> 00:09:51.610
This way, a lot of impurities can be removed.

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:54.860
The local guild provided them for us quickly.

00:09:54.870 --> 00:10:00.450
However, the guild apparently doesn't know where the sand was added to the salt.

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:05.370
Are you saying... the salt is being intercepted somewhere?

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:06.950
It's such a nuisance.

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:09.370
Hey, what are you doing here?

00:10:09.370 --> 00:10:10.640
Tan-tan...

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:16.130
This is a serious threat.

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:16.780
What?

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:21.210
Salt is essential for life.

00:10:21.210 --> 00:10:24.370
People can't live without salt.

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:26.470
Well... yeah...

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:32.110
Rising salt prices are alarming, if you take a long term view.

00:10:32.110 --> 00:10:35.420
Okay... but...

00:10:35.420 --> 00:10:39.610
The specialists must've noticed by now.

00:10:39.900 --> 00:10:43.200
Like last time, when the Section of Government Inspection was already working on the case.

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:44.990
But what if they haven't noticed?

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:50.740
More importantly, aren't you supposed to be thinking about how to avoid dismissal?

00:10:50.740 --> 00:10:51.990
There!

00:10:51.990 --> 00:10:52.880
Where?

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:55.300
All I need to do is render distinguished service.

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:57.890
If I find out where the sand is being added to the salt,

00:10:57.890 --> 00:11:02.030
understand the situation, and prevent salt price inflation,

00:11:02.030 --> 00:11:05.310
then that should suffice to avoid getting fired.

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:09.900
So why don't you give it a go?

00:11:09.900 --> 00:11:11.930
You're unbeatable.

00:11:11.930 --> 00:11:13.180
Really.

00:11:13.180 --> 00:11:14.370
Tan-tan...

00:11:14.370 --> 00:11:15.700
Though...

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:19.460
This seems really familiar.

00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:21.780
That's what I thought too.

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:25.960
The situation seems much too similar to the counterfeiting case.

00:11:27.170 --> 00:11:28.790
There's no mistake about it.

00:11:29.150 --> 00:11:33.420
The same person is pulling the strings this time as well.

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:35.610
Not even a second thought?

00:11:35.610 --> 00:11:39.990
No. From the outset, I thought it was very well planned.

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:46.430
He distracted us with counterfeit coins and forgeries, while intending to make his profit on salt?

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:49.950
Yes, you can make guaranteed profits on salt.

00:11:50.650 --> 00:11:51.890
We should take action immediately!

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:52.940
No.

00:11:53.410 --> 00:11:56.860
Your Highness should not deal with this.

00:11:56.860 --> 00:12:02.070
The guild and your officials should be able to handle such a trifling matter.

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:07.700
Your Highness needs to consider something else about this case.

00:12:08.090 --> 00:12:09.450
What's that?

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:14.720
What if I said this salt incident is part of larger plan?

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:24.850
Shuurei-san!

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:28.600
What a coincidence.

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:29.830
Seiga-san.

00:12:30.330 --> 00:12:35.100
You two must be really close if you're together on a day off.

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:36.500
It's not like that.

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:40.130
I only ran into Tan-tan by chance. I'm just doing a bit of research.

00:12:40.130 --> 00:12:41.470
Research?

00:12:41.470 --> 00:12:42.080
Yes.

00:12:42.080 --> 00:12:43.110
Hey,

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:45.650
are you getting Seiga-kun involved into this as well?

00:12:46.560 --> 00:12:47.930
I don't mind.

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:50.050
I've got time.

00:12:50.050 --> 00:12:52.250
I'd like to hear about it, if you don't mind.

00:12:54.380 --> 00:12:55.370
Well...

00:12:57.080 --> 00:12:58.680
I see.

00:12:58.680 --> 00:13:02.000
I agree with you that the salt case needs to be investigated.

00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:04.880
But there are too many uncertainties.

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:09.320
Besides, if something is happening during transport,

00:13:09.320 --> 00:13:12.220
can you determine where by working here in Kiyou?

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:16.020
I think I can do something about that.

00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:19.330
I'm worried about you, Shuurei-san.

00:13:20.080 --> 00:13:21.920
You have less than half a month now.

00:13:22.910 --> 00:13:25.530
Personally, I think you should first find

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:29.670
a reliable way to avoid getting dismissed.

00:13:33.670 --> 00:13:36.500
Well, from your expression, that's not going to happen, is it?

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:40.790
Impossible. I told her the same thing,
but she insists she's made her mind up.

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:43.000
Once her mind is set, she won't budge.

00:13:44.070 --> 00:13:46.820
So, where were you heading?

00:13:46.820 --> 00:13:49.380
I thought I'd better hear the real story.

00:13:50.070 --> 00:13:53.390
Were you, by any chance, thinking of visiting Prime Minister Tei's wife?

00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:55.830
How did you guess that?

00:13:55.830 --> 00:13:59.150
Prime Minister Tei has assisted you before.

00:13:59.150 --> 00:14:03.830
Besides, I hear that his wife was
originally in the Merchants Guild.

00:14:03.830 --> 00:14:07.530
So if you're going to talk to anyone about salt, I thought it'd be her.

00:14:08.670 --> 00:14:11.410
If you don't mind, may I come with you?

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:14.290
I'm also concerned, now that I've heard about it.

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:15.860
Yeah, by all means.

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:23.010
Amazing. What's this room?

00:14:23.010 --> 00:14:24.250
Impressive.

00:14:24.610 --> 00:14:26.150
Sorry to have kept you waiting.

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:31.910
I'm glad you've come, Shuurei-dono. Are these your friends?

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:43.020
That... Was that your invention, Rin-san?

00:14:43.340 --> 00:14:44.450
Yes.

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:46.970
I'm glad they've been so useful.

00:14:46.970 --> 00:14:49.900
You've come about the salt, haven't you, Shuurei-dono?

00:14:49.900 --> 00:14:52.600
Umm, you can tell?

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:56.410
Does that mean Yuushun-san knows about it already?

00:14:56.710 --> 00:14:58.470
Of course he does.

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:02.520
But this is not my husband's responsibility.

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:05.190
It's hard to decide to what extent the government should get involved.

00:15:05.190 --> 00:15:09.170
So, what do you want to ask me?

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:14.550
Is there anything I can do about this case?

00:15:14.550 --> 00:15:20.440
If there's nothing I can do, then I promise I won't get involved any further.

00:15:22.030 --> 00:15:26.440
Something about the last case has made you think more about your actions?

00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:29.900
Do what you can, and what you're asked to do first.

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:32.880
Only then can you think about what you want to do.

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:37.580
Still, I thought I could do all this just by myself.

00:15:38.590 --> 00:15:43.710
Perhaps your strengths are your luck, connections, and openness to advice.

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:47.640
Particularly your great luck and your fortune with people. They're simply incredible.

00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:50.210
Not everyone is blessed with those things.

00:15:50.770 --> 00:15:55.180
But what allows you to draw on your luck and bind people to you

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:57.030
is your willingness to accept advice.

00:15:57.480 --> 00:16:03.310
Because of that, many people care about you and try to help you out.

00:16:03.740 --> 00:16:07.440
So, is there anything she can do?

00:16:07.880 --> 00:16:08.840
Yes.

00:16:08.840 --> 00:16:14.130
If we can get Shuurei-dono's help, we can probably solve this much more quickly.

00:16:14.130 --> 00:16:14.820
Which means-

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:20.830
If you ignore the time it will take to solve this case, you can sort it out eventually without her help?

00:16:25.310 --> 00:16:27.260
I understand what you're trying to say.

00:16:27.260 --> 00:16:33.470
You're right, so I'll leave it to Shuurei-dono to decide if she wants to help.

00:16:38.530 --> 00:16:40.510
Please allow me to assist you.

00:16:45.710 --> 00:16:49.720
It's unusual for you to ask me for a favor, Shuurei-dono.

00:16:49.720 --> 00:16:51.990
Yes, it's about salt.

00:16:51.990 --> 00:16:53.490
Salt?

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:56.250
Salt is Ranshuu's specialty.

00:16:56.250 --> 00:17:00.120
I thought Ran-shogun would be able to lend us a hand.

00:17:00.430 --> 00:17:05.750
Could you find out if anyone has applied for new permits to manufacture salt in the last few months,

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:10.760
or has attempted to purchase saltworks in Ranshuu?

00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:13.170
Of course.

00:17:13.690 --> 00:17:15.130
Thank you so much!

00:17:15.550 --> 00:17:18.720
That's nothing for me.

00:17:19.290 --> 00:17:22.390
Here you are, Shuurei-dono. A little souvenir.

00:17:23.130 --> 00:17:24.740
Thank you.

00:17:25.530 --> 00:17:28.860
Wow, peaches!

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:33.610
But... we won't be able to finish all these.

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:36.440
Come by again.

00:17:36.440 --> 00:17:40.720
Next time I'll have all your favorite
sweets ready for you, Shuurei-dono.

00:17:48.790 --> 00:17:49.500
Huh?

00:17:50.410 --> 00:17:52.410
Who would be here so early in the morning?

00:17:58.200 --> 00:17:59.900
I thought you'd be here.

00:17:59.900 --> 00:18:00.890
Shuurei!

00:18:01.270 --> 00:18:03.410
I suppose we can afford to do this once in a while.

00:18:03.410 --> 00:18:05.640
Would you like to eat breakfast together?

00:18:07.590 --> 00:18:10.980
Sh-Shuurei! All for me?

00:18:12.340 --> 00:18:13.440
Riou!

00:18:13.440 --> 00:18:15.940
Why don't you join us too?

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:19.740
I was trying to leave you two alone.

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:22.270
Riou-kun! Why are you here?

00:18:22.270 --> 00:18:25.070
No, I mean, I was worried about you!

00:18:25.070 --> 00:18:26.840
Where have you been?

00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:28.900
Ah, well...

00:18:29.820 --> 00:18:31.390
What's going on?

00:18:31.390 --> 00:18:34.020
I'm sorry, but I can't tell you anything right now.

00:18:35.910 --> 00:18:38.260
I don't know anything about him either!

00:18:41.040 --> 00:18:43.260
I promise, I'll tell you everything one day.

00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:47.890
Fine. I won't ask you anything for now.

00:18:49.090 --> 00:18:50.770
Then let's eat!

00:18:51.220 --> 00:18:53.420
Thanks for breakfast!

00:18:58.830 --> 00:18:59.530
Delicious!

00:19:03.850 --> 00:19:06.740
Oh, peaches are my favorite.

00:19:06.740 --> 00:19:11.590
Yes, Ran-shogun gave me a lot, so I brought some.

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:14.500
From Shuuei...

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:19.560
I felt like he was asking me to bring them to you.

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:23.530
Because Shuuei's a nice guy...

00:19:32.540 --> 00:19:37.280
With Seiga's help, Shuurei worked hard, sacrificing her sleep,

00:19:37.280 --> 00:19:42.030
to solve the salt case and avoid being dismissed as an official.

00:19:42.470 --> 00:19:45.670
We've got most of the evidence.
I think we're going to make it in time.

00:19:45.670 --> 00:19:49.890
The report and evidence required to press charges are complete.

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:53.790
I'm sorry I dragged you around for so many days, Seiga-san.

00:19:54.620 --> 00:19:57.000
Ah, don't worry about it.

00:19:58.190 --> 00:20:01.550
Oh, I noticed something interesting.

00:20:01.550 --> 00:20:04.550
I've been tracking the salt transport routes.

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:10.060
More than half of the salt passes through
Chin family territory before entering Kiyou.

00:20:10.710 --> 00:20:12.390
The Chin family?

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:15.530
I think it's worth looking into.

00:20:15.530 --> 00:20:17.200
What's wrong with you?!

00:20:17.770 --> 00:20:20.320
What are you doing in the Civil Service library?

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:23.700
Oh, Hakumei-kun, you seem busy as usual.

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:24.700
Well then,

00:20:25.030 --> 00:20:27.080
I'll be leaving first.

00:20:30.530 --> 00:20:31.580
Who was that?

00:20:31.580 --> 00:20:33.210
I've never seen him before.

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:35.810
He's called Riku Seiga-san.

00:20:35.810 --> 00:20:38.340
Oh, he's from the Riku family.

00:20:38.780 --> 00:20:42.000
A Riku family member is a joukan?

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:42.810
What?

00:20:42.810 --> 00:20:47.390
The Riku family has a long history.
They're even related to the royal family.

00:20:47.630 --> 00:20:50.390
So he's an heir to a distinguished family...

00:20:50.640 --> 00:20:54.450
But, you can't compare his family's rank to the Kou family.

00:20:54.450 --> 00:20:55.740
Don't be intimidated by that.

00:20:55.740 --> 00:20:59.020
Anyway! What are you doing?

00:20:59.020 --> 00:21:00.170
What am I doing?

00:21:00.170 --> 00:21:02.400
That's what I'm asking you!

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:06.590
Do you realize you're this close to being dismissed?

00:21:06.590 --> 00:21:07.820
But look at you.

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:10.410
First you were busy taking care of the other joukan,

00:21:10.680 --> 00:21:12.160
and now you're doing research in here.

00:21:12.590 --> 00:21:15.540
What are you thinking, neglecting to find yourself a job?!

00:21:17.080 --> 00:21:19.160
Thanks for caring.

00:21:19.160 --> 00:21:21.420
I'm really happy, Hakumei-kun.

00:21:22.930 --> 00:21:25.900
Oh, so you have something in mind?

00:21:25.900 --> 00:21:30.550
I expect you've lined up a job that's certain so you can avoid dismissal, right?

00:21:30.550 --> 00:21:34.060
Umm... not "certain," but...

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:36.080
What?!

00:21:36.850 --> 00:21:40.980
What chance do you think you have, if you don't have anything certain to assure your position?!

00:21:40.980 --> 00:21:44.320
I'm planning to be ready on time!

00:21:44.320 --> 00:21:47.990
Please, Hakumei-kun, let me finish this.

00:21:52.240 --> 00:21:54.950
You passed with a higher grade than me.

00:21:55.350 --> 00:21:59.980
You've got a responsibility to remain as an official, no matter what.

00:21:59.980 --> 00:22:06.260
But... I have no right to interfere with your decision, if you're sure about it.

00:22:07.950 --> 00:22:09.640
You'd better do a good job.

00:22:10.780 --> 00:22:13.150
Thank you, Hakumei-kun.

00:22:21.060 --> 00:22:22.940
Oh, Youshun-san.

00:22:22.940 --> 00:22:28.070
Honestly, you two work too hard. Take a break.

00:22:29.860 --> 00:22:30.870
Please.

00:22:32.340 --> 00:22:33.660
Thank you.

00:22:33.660 --> 00:22:37.040
Is Suou-san not here again today?

00:22:37.040 --> 00:22:41.030
That's right, I haven't seen him for a few days now.

00:22:41.030 --> 00:22:42.580
What in the world is he up to?

00:22:42.580 --> 00:22:43.930
As I feared...

00:22:45.200 --> 00:22:48.530
Was that rumor true?

00:22:49.400 --> 00:22:52.220
What rumor?

00:22:55.100 --> 00:22:58.350
I heard that Suou-san's father...

00:22:58.940 --> 00:23:01.440
died recently.

00:23:01.440 --> 00:23:02.400
What?

00:23:02.400 --> 00:23:03.960
When was that?!

00:23:03.960 --> 00:23:08.280
If I remember correctly, the day before our last day off.

00:23:10.750 --> 00:23:13.760
If I ask, will you play a piece for me?

00:23:14.280 --> 00:23:17.500
Nothing, really.

00:23:17.540 --> 00:23:20.770
He was acting strange back then because...

00:24:45.390 --> 00:24:47.130
With Seiga-san's help,

00:24:47.130 --> 00:24:50.200
we're finally starting to see the whole picture about the rise in salt prices,

00:24:50.200 --> 00:24:52.540
as well as the person who's behind it.

00:24:52.540 --> 00:24:54.430
The case is solved.

00:24:54.430 --> 00:24:57.300
Hold on! Seiga-san, what are you...
